ed": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Now a regression test, then I'll run it along with the existing suite.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`. I tested this by calling the function directly. pytest isn't installed here, so I haven't run the test files.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, and Python's `round()` rounds that stored value, so it goes down. `round()` also rounds an exact half to the even digit (`0.125` \u2192 `0.12`), which breaks the \"half up\" rule in the docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): turn the float into a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`, which gives the short number you'd type (`\"2.675\"`). Then round to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and convert back to a float, so callers still get the same type.\n\n**Direct calls:** these all came out as expected: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `0.135\u21920.14`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`. `add_vat(10)` still gives `12.0` and `split(10.00, 3)` still gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`.\n\n**Regression test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py` with those same cases. It will run once pytest is installed.\n\n**Remaining issue:** `add_vat` multiplies before rounding (`x * 1.2`), and that multiplication can itself leave a tiny float error. If the product lands just below a half-cent, it will still round down. Fully fixing that means doing the VAT math in `Decimal` as well, which I didn't change.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 250543, "requests_cache_write": 7447, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1304436, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2151, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial6", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 8, "score": 1.0, "st